{"type":"npc","name":"Archival Monitor","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":210,"temp":0,"max":210,"details":""},"ac":{"value":30,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":20}],"details":"wasteland walker"},"immunities":[{"type":"fire","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","luxan"],"details":"Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"},"level":{"value":11},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Archival monitors appear as large reptiles with a pronounced crystalline crest protruding from their heads. This crest is not only ornamental but also contains the collective memories of their ancestors, allowing them to remember events and experiences from the distant past. Archival monitors typically wander lost ruins, following ancient migratory routes and erecting grand illusory structures when they come across an important historical site.</p><p>The knowledge that each archival monitor carries is a priceless treasure to archaeologists, historians, and adventurers alike. However, their ancestral memories also include instances where others have attempted to exploit them for knowledge or hunt them for crests. As a result, they are very slow to trust. Still, archival monitors value the preservation of their traditions, and they are sometimes willing to share their wealth of experience with those who prove themselves through an appropriate task or trial.</p><p>All archival monitors share ancestral memories, including arcane formulas for manipulating light using crests. They use these formulas to great effect in defending their homes from violent or otherwise unsavory intruders, burning them with focused light beams or imprisoning them in a cage before slowly roasting them alive.</p><h2>Peaceful Pilgrimages</h2><p>Strong enough to defend themselves against most threats—and meaning no harm toward those with no harm to offer—archival monitors can serve as islands of safety in otherwise dangerous lands. As they wend their long circuit through treacherous ruins, an archival monitor can pick up an escort of smaller creatures too weak to defend themselves. To those with an interest in history, no traveling companion is more congenial than an archival monitor reminiscing about the past.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 175/390/720 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Arcana, Athletics, Lore [Genealogy])</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, burning barbs, constitution, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (fire, vitality), fire, fire shield, intelligence, light, mind, mind shield, sensory (low-light vision, scent), spells (Arcane: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.ZYoC630tNGutgbE0]{Hypercognition}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.WBmvzNDfpwka3qT4]{Light}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.D442XMADp01qJ7Cs]{Mindlink}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.HBJPsonQnWcC3qdX]{Mirage}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.SwUiVavHKMWG7t5K]{Truespeech}), strength, throwing, wild, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Benjamin Sulzer","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":6},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":6},"int":{"mod":6},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":22,"senses":[{"type":"low-light-vision"},{"type":"scent","acuity":"imprecise","range":30}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":24,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":21,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":21},"arcana":{"base":23},"athletics":{"base":23}},"traits":{"value":["beast"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"lg"}}},"_id":"CQDGfdZwNisX21JR","